<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arauco War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1536–1818</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Arauco War was the long conflict between the Spanish and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mapuche">Mapuche</a> of south-central Chile. It began with the Spanish invasion of the 1540s; the Mapuche killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-de-valdivia">Pedro de Valdivia</a> at Tucapel in 1553 and destroyed the southern Spanish towns after Curalaba in 1598. The Biobío river became a fortified frontier, and the war shaped the military character of colonial Chile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arauco-war.jpg" alt="Arauco War" width="320" height="437" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tomas Lopez compuesto por el mapa manuscrito de Poncho Chileno, Madrid 1777 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mapa_Chile_Espa%C3%B1oles_y_Araucanos.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
